{% extends 'pages/communities/sagamok/members-first-plan-layout.html.twig' %}
{% set plan_key = 'homes' %}{% set plan_short = 'Homes and infrastructure' %}{% set plan_eyebrow = 'Priority 4' %}
{% set plan_title = 'Homes, water and infrastructure that get delivered' %}
{% set plan_description = 'Replace scattered promises with one funded pipeline for lots, homes, repairs, water, roads, buildings and long-term maintenance.' %}
{% block plan_content %}
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">The outcome</p><h2>Members can see where every project stands and what will open next.</h2><p class="plan-lede">Housing and infrastructure become a delivery system: verified need, serviced land, design, funding, procurement, construction, occupancy and maintenance.</p></header><div class="plan-grid plan-grid--3"><div class="plan-card"><h3>One queue</h3><p>Clear eligibility, priority rules, application status and appeal.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>One project pipeline</h3><p>Every lot, home, repair and infrastructure project uses the same status stages.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Whole-life cost</h3><p>Capital approval includes operation, maintenance, renewal and staffing.</p></div></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Public baseline</p><h2>Housing direction exists. Delivery status must follow.</h2></header><div class="plan-grid"><div class="plan-card"><h3>422-home objective</h3><p>Council minutes of April 22, 2025 recorded a ten-year objective and a conditional package of lots, homes, repairs and foundations.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Up to 30 homes</h3><p>Motion 2025/10 #17 directed planning and procurement for up to 30 homes in 2026 and 2027, with budgets, designs, locations and contracts to return.</p></div></div><p class="plan-note"><strong>Required now:</strong> the returned package, confirmed funding, serviced-lot capacity, water capacity, procurement status and completion dates.</p></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Year One commitments</p><h2>Publish and deliver the pipeline.</h2></header><div class="plan-commitments"><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Verified housing-needs baseline</h3><p>Count households by need, unit type, urgency, accessibility and preferred tenure without exposing identities.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Public project schedule</h3><p>Show each project at concept, design, funded, tendered, construction, complete or occupied.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Serviced-land plan</h3><p>Match lots with water, wastewater, roads, power, drainage and legal readiness.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Repair and mould program</h3><p>Set triage times, inspection standards, scope approval, completion targets and recurrence checks.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Water reliability plan</h3><p>Publish capacity, pressure, leaks, treatment constraints, capital works and emergency response.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Asset maintenance system</h3><p>Inventory buildings and infrastructure with condition, service life, maintenance schedule and renewal cost.</p></article></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Quarterly measures</p><h2>Count delivery, not announcements.</h2></header><div class="plan-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Homes</th><th>Repairs</th><th>Infrastructure</th><th>Cost and schedule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Lots serviced, starts, completions and occupancies</td><td>Requests, inspections, work orders and completion time</td><td>Water interruptions, pressure events and leaks repaired</td><td>Budget, spent, forecast, milestone and variance</td></tr><tr><td>Wait-list movement by need category</td><td>Repeat mould or repair cases</td><td>Assets inspected and maintenance completed</td><td>Contracts awarded and local benefit</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="plan-decision"><h2>Decisions members make</h2><ul><li>Which housing needs come first?</li><li>What balance of rental, ownership, rent-to-own, Elders and supportive housing is required?</li><li>What information should every applicant be able to see about the queue?</li><li>Which capital projects pause when operating and maintenance funding is missing?</li></ul></section>
